+Reports and applied proposals are all kept (old reports and minutes move into `99 Archive`, below). **Backups look after themselves (BL-323; Alan, 14-10-2026):** a daily **Tidy up**, after the backup and the zip, removes only files creaite wrote (matched by their exact name in their own folder), never the newest of a kind, never in the development repository, not when that day's backup or zip failed, and never from a process an ask creaite run started (`backup.ask_run`: the live server's flag or `system/guard/run.json`; Alan, 14-10-2026); it runs from the session start rule in Alan's own Claude Code session and the live server's daily job; it can't be undone, and Health shows the last run. **Restore from a backup** is in Settings › Health (a dashboard-only, token-checked route that accepts only a zip name from the server's own list) and in cx-setup. The rules (`backups.*`, the same locally and in OneDrive): daily database backups and daily zips every day for 30 days, then one a week (the Monday's) for a year, then one a month (the first) for good; apply, undo, revert and migrate copies 14 days; dashboard snapshots 30 days, then one a month (the `flow-*.json` files for good); release zips: the installed one and the two before it; update backups: the last three; file-change backups 90 days (undo of an older change then says the backup has gone). Other exceptions: ask creaite keeps only the 10 most recent chats in `system/staging/ask/` (BL-32; starting an 11th deletes the oldest), the debug log keeps only the last seven days (BL-102; the first entry of a new day deletes older files), and the run usage log (`system/staging/run-usage.jsonl`, #197) is kept for good (about 200 bytes a run, counts only).
 
-**Archiving (BL-10, BL-03) deletes nothing.** Once a day, after the daily backup (session start, and the live server's daily job after Tidy up), closed or cancelled actions and RAID items, and done or dropped promises, closed `archive.after_months` (6) months ago are flagged archived through `tracker.py apply`: automatic, as the flag is undoable; decisions, milestones and open items never are; editing an item un-archives it; never from an ask creaite run. Weekly and client reports, minutes and Steerco one-pagers older than `archive.reports_after_months` (12) are offered once a month in Settings › Health and, on Alan's yes on the approval card, moved into the engagement's own `_Archive` (the portfolio's minutes into the portfolio's `_Archive`) by `tracker.py apply` (never by ask creaite), and back, only on the live server's own approval card. Restoring a project leaves items archived for their age archived. Transcripts, agendas, documents and applied proposals are never archived. **Delete note (#124; Alan, 15-10-2026)** also moves into `_Archive`: one note (`notes`, a `.md` directly in its notes folder) into its engagement's (or the portfolio's) `_Archive/<notes folder>/`, and back (`notes_back`, under its old name, or `-2` and so on if a note has taken it), only by `tracker.py apply` on the live server's own approval card after Alan's confirm box, only the version he confirmed; never from an ask creaite run. `tracker.py` makes these moves (and a report's move back) only with the card's one-time approval, so a proposal written into staging by hand is refused; such a proposal could still remove or copy a note, undoably.
